WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:10.550
This is the debrief for Independent QC, where you double-program a demographics table and report every disagreement with production.

2
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.950
First, build an independent QC table from the specification.

3
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.690
Second, compare it with production cell by cell, using a tolerance.

4
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.930
Third, report one row per discrepancy, and none when the tables agree.

5
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.660
qc_demographics() finds the arms from the data, instead of assuming their names.

6
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.360
For each arm, it takes that arm's subjects only.

7
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.740
Then it computes n, the mean age, and its standard deviation.

8
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:39.060
pct_female divides by the subjects in that arm, which is exactly where production went wrong.

9
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.630
compare_tables() looks at every column the two tables share, except arm.

10
00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:50.930
It starts from an empty data frame with the report's columns, so a clean comparison returns zero rows of the right shape.

11
00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.110
Then it walks every arm and every column, cell by cell.

12
00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:59.370
A difference counts only when it exceeds the tolerance, so floating-point noise is never reported.

13
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.680
Three mistakes account for most failed attempts.

14
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.950
Comparing with == flags differences that are only rounding noise, and the tolerance check fails.

15
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.740
Checking only the column you know is wrong misses discrepancies in a different production table.

16
00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.950
And returning NULL when everything matches, instead of an empty data frame, fails the clean check.

17
00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.100
This solution passes all seven checks.

18
00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:29.100
The validator self-test runs this exact code against every one of them, so what you see here is what the boss grades.

19
00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.080
Your own solution can look different.

20
00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.460
What matters is that it passes the same checks.
